  "created": "2022-01-12T17:09:03.833Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Movement based on where you are looking is great for new players who need help getting to places. However, for players looking for advanced controls, having a system where the player can make subtle movements independent of view could make the experience richer. Like in games, if you are being chased by another player you don't want to look directly at them as you are moving, as you would run directly into them.\nI also understand that in a game where \"forward\" is hard to track, having movement follow the headset is an intuitive solution.\nI do have alternative solutions, but without understanding how things work the best I can do is try to snowball this with an idea.\nFor FBT users, give them the option to use the hip tracker as a way to track \"forward.\" Movement is more consistent as your head is not always telling of what direction you're moving in. This would be set in FBT calibration. However, this only works in FBT situations.\nI could not think of any decent 3-point tracking solutions. I'm hoping someone else can.",
